IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art8-register`
IMPORT `g3-art9-restricted-section`

-- g3-art10-public-access.l4: Article 10 (Public access): the duty to publish the public parts of the register on a website for inspection without charge (10(1)),
-- the Minister's power to provide for other access on payment (10(2)), which parts of the register are public (10(3)), and the Commissioner's power to designate a matter
-- as not public where safety or security would be significantly put at risk (10(4), 10(5)).
-- The Commissioner's consideration of a risk, the specification of a manner of access and the amount of a charge are inputs.

§ `Article 10 -- Public access`

§§ `Article 10(1): publication on a website`

-- The Article states no time within which the public parts are to be made available, so no WITHIN is written.
-- src:288 | (1) The Commissioner must make the public parts of the register available to the public on a website for inspection without charge.
@ref Article 10(1) (src:288)
@export The Commissioner must make the public parts of the register available to the public on a website for inspection without charge (Article 10(1)); stands until the Commissioner does so
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 10(1) the Commissioner must make the public parts of the register available on a website` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST `make the public parts of the register available to the public on a website for inspection without charge`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "Article 10(1): the public parts of the register were not made available to the public on a website for inspection without charge"

§§ `Article 10(2): other manners of access, on payment`

-- src:289 | (2) The Minister may by Order provide for the Commissioner to make the public parts of the register available in any other specified manner, to the public or to such description of persons as may be specified, on payment of –
@ref Article 10(2) (src:289)
@export The Minister may by Order provide for the Commissioner to make the public parts of the register available in any other specified manner, on payment of a charge (Article 10(2))
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 10(2) the Minister may by Order provide for other access to the public parts of the register` MEANS
    `the Minister may by Order prescribe` `another manner in which the public parts of the register are made available, on payment of a charge`

-- src:290 | (a) a specified charge; or
@ref Article 10(2)(a) (src:290)
GIVEN content IS A `Content of an Order under Article 10(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 10(2)(a) the Order requires payment of a specified charge` content MEANS
    content's `payment required` EQUALS JUST `a specified charge`

-- src:291 | (b) a charge determined and published by the Commissioner.
@ref Article 10(2)(b) (src:291)
GIVEN content IS A `Content of an Order under Article 10(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 10(2)(b) the Order requires payment of a charge determined and published by the Commissioner` content MEANS
    content's `payment required` EQUALS JUST `a charge determined and published by the Commissioner`

-- The Order must provide for access "on payment of (a) a specified charge; or (b) a charge determined and published by the Commissioner": an Order that provides for another
-- manner of access without payment is not one the power reaches.
-- src:289 | (2) The Minister may by Order provide for the Commissioner to make the public parts of the register available in any other specified manner, to the public or to such description of persons as may be specified, on payment of –
-- src:290 | (a) a specified charge; or
-- src:291 | (b) a charge determined and published by the Commissioner.
@ref Article 10(2) (src:289-291)
@export Whether an Order provides for access to the public parts of the register in another specified manner on payment of a charge within Article 10(2)(a) or (b)
GIVEN content IS A `Content of an Order under Article 10(2)` @desc What the Order provides: whether it specifies another manner of access, and the charge it requires, if any
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 10(2) the Order provides for another specified manner of access on payment of a charge within (a) or (b)` content MEANS
        content's `specifies another manner in which the public parts are made available`
    AND (   `Art 10(2)(a) the Order requires payment of a specified charge` content
         OR `Art 10(2)(b) the Order requires payment of a charge determined and published by the Commissioner` content)

§§ `Article 10(4) and (5): a matter the Commissioner designates as not public`

-- F3.3.  "in relation to a particular registered charity" -- a "registered charity" (Article 1) is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section; the historic section is
-- excluded on the reading taken, though its contents are public (10(3)(c)).  The Commissioner's consideration is an input.
@ref Article 10(4) (fork F3.3)
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F3.3 reading A: a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only` standing MEANS
    `the standing is that of a registered charity` standing

@ref Article 10(4) (fork F3.3)
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F3.3 reading B: a registered charity includes an entity formerly registered and entered in the historic section` standing MEANS
    `the standing is that of a registered charity` standing OR standing EQUALS `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`

@ref Article 10(4) (fork F3.3)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      standing IS A `Standing on the register`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the standing is within Article 10(4)'s reach` interp standing MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `reach of Article 10(4)`
    WHEN `a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only` THEN `F3.3 reading A: a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only` standing
    WHEN `a registered charity includes an entity formerly registered and entered in the historic section` THEN `F3.3 reading B: a registered charity includes an entity formerly registered and entered in the historic section` standing

-- src:296 | (4) Paragraph (5) applies if the Commissioner considers, in relation to a particular registered charity, that the safety or security of any person, property or premises would be significantly put at risk by public access to a matter entered on any section of the register in respect of that charity.
@ref Article 10(4) (src:296)
@export Whether Article 10(5) applies: the Commissioner considers that the safety or security of any person, property or premises would be significantly put at risk by public access to a matter entered on a section of the register in respect of a particular registered charity
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10 (whether Article 10(4) reaches an entity that has been deregistered); the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity the matter is entered about, with its standing on the register
      `the Commissioner considers that public access to the matter would significantly put safety or security at risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Commissioner's consideration; it is the Commissioner's own and is supplied
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 10(4) paragraph (5) applies` interp `the entity` `the Commissioner considers that public access to the matter would significantly put safety or security at risk` MEANS
        `the Commissioner considers that public access to the matter would significantly put safety or security at risk`
    AND `the standing is within Article 10(4)'s reach` interp (`the entity`'s `standing on the register`)

-- src:297 | (5) The Commissioner may designate that matter as not being a public part of the register, in relation to that registered charity.
@ref Article 10(5) (src:297)
@export The Commissioner may designate a matter entered in respect of a registered charity as not being a public part of the register (Article 10(5)); available only where Article 10(4) applies; a permission, so not designating is no breach
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10 (whether Article 10(4) reaches an entity that has been deregistered); the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity the matter is entered about, with its standing on the register
      `the Commissioner considers that public access to the matter would significantly put safety or security at risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Commissioner's consideration; it is the Commissioner's own and is supplied
      matter IS A `Matter entered on the register` @desc The matter to be designated
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 10(5) the Commissioner may designate the matter as not a public part of the register` interp `the entity` `the Commissioner considers that public access to the matter would significantly put safety or security at risk` matter MEANS
    IF `Art 10(4) paragraph (5) applies` interp `the entity` `the Commissioner considers that public access to the matter would significantly put safety or security at risk`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY `designate a matter as not being a public part of the register` matter
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `Article 10(3): which parts of the register are public`

-- The matter is in the section the entity is in.  General section: public.  Restricted section: only its public elements (Article 9(1)).  Historic section: public.
-- All "subject to paragraph (5)": a matter the Commissioner has designated as not public, in relation to that charity, where Article 10(4) lets the Commissioner do so.
-- A designation outside Article 10(4)'s reach is not an exercise of the power and does not take the matter out of a public part.
-- src:292 | (3) For the purpose of paragraphs (1) and (2), the public parts of the register are, subject to paragraph (5) –
-- src:293 | (a) the general section;
-- src:294 | (b) the public elements of the restricted section, within the meaning of Article 9(1); and
-- src:295 | (c) the historic section.
@ref Article 10(3) (src:292-295)
@export Whether a matter entered on the register for an entity is in a public part of the register (Article 10(3)): the general section, the public elements of the restricted section, the historic section, less what the Commissioner has validly designated as not public (Article 10(5))
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10 (whether Article 10(4) reaches an entity that has been deregistered); the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity the matter is entered about, with its standing on the register (the matter is in the section its standing names)
      matter IS A `Matter entered on the register` @desc The matter: the registered name, the registration number, an item of Article 8(3) or 8(5), the summary of the reasons, or an element an Order prescribes
      `the Commissioner has designated the matter as not a public part of the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has designated the matter under Article 10(5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 10(3) the matter is in a public part of the register` interp `the entity` matter `the Commissioner has designated the matter as not a public part of the register` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section named by the standing` (`the entity`'s `standing on the register`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST section THEN
        inPublicPart section AND NOT designatedAndValid
    WHERE
        inPublicPart section MEANS
            CONSIDER section
            WHEN `the general section` THEN TRUE                                                                  -- 10(3)(a)
            WHEN `the restricted section` THEN `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` matter   -- 10(3)(b)
            WHEN `the historic section` THEN TRUE                                                                 -- 10(3)(c)
        designatedAndValid MEANS
                `the Commissioner has designated the matter as not a public part of the register`
            AND `the standing is within Article 10(4)'s reach` interp (`the entity`'s `standing on the register`)
